notes.body:
As Le might be [up to 3 bytes](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smart_card_application_protocol_data_unit#APDU_message_command-response_pair),
shouldn't be something like this here?
```suggestion:-1+0
				proto_tree_add_item(sim_tree, hf_le, tvb, offset, tvb_reported_length_remaining(tvb, offset), ENC_NA);
				offset += tvb_reported_length_remaining(tvb, offset);
```

According to the GlobalPlatform Card Specification the last 00 byte should not be present when more blocks expected.
![Screenshot_2026-02-05_at_17.24.02](/uploads/6f36994ee10894b73baf126d818bbbaf/Screenshot_2026-02-05_at_17.24.02.png){width=836 height=405}

I will add a warning for this.
![Screenshot_2026-02-05_at_17.28.33](/uploads/3dc784415d0fb7c0bb188227179008a4/Screenshot_2026-02-05_at_17.28.33.png){width=794 height=440}

